# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

Gives one person access to an Ory Network project through an invite.

Ory emails the invite to `email`. The person accepts the invite with a Console account that uses the same address, and then has the configured `role` on the project. `status` is `pending` until the person accepts the invite, and `accepted` after. See [Roles and permissions](https://www.ory.com/docs/console/roles-and-permissions) for what each role can do. To give access to every project in a workspace, use `ory_workspace_member`.

-> **Plan:** Available on all Ory Network plans. Members and pending invites count as collaborator seats, so the seat limit of the plan applies.

~> **Authentication:** The Ory Console API accepts member and invite requests only from a signed-in Console user, and answers a workspace API key with HTTP 401. Run `ory auth` and set `workspace_api_key` to the access token, as [Managing a project without a workspace API key](https://registry.terraform.io/providers/ory/ory/latest/docs#managing-a-project-without-a-workspace-api-key) describes. The user must be an owner of the project or of its workspace.

